  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Characteristics of aromatic compounds include:<br />- Must be Cyclic and planar<br />- Must have <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></math>&nbsp;electrons <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></mrow></mfenced></math><br />- Resist Addition but Prefer Substitution.<br />- Must Possess Resonance Energy.<br />Due to severe non-bonded interactions between the internal hydrogen (as shown in figure), the ring assumes non-planar geometry in 10-annulene, hence, it is not an aromatic compound.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/1384eaaf-d2a0-42b0-84e6-b770a8a196aa-9755187_S.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 213px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
